Live data (public feeds)
  Weather and air quality by Open-Meteo, https://open-meteo.com, CC BY 4.0 (credited in the
    weather panel).
  Weather alerts from the US National Weather Service, https://www.weather.gov (public domain).
  Bike data from Bluebikes' GBFS feed (https://bluebikes.com/system-data), provided under the
    Bluebikes Data License Agreement.
  MIT shuttle data from MIT's Passio GO GTFS-realtime feed. Bus predictions and timetables from
    the MBTA V3 API (https://www.mbta.com/developers), under the MBTA's developer terms. Lucent
    is not endorsed by the MBTA.
  Aircraft positions from adsb.fi, https://adsb.fi (open data for non-commercial use, credited
    in the planes panel), with adsb.lol (ODbL) as the fallback. Flight routes from adsbdb,
    https://www.adsbdb.com, and hexdb.io.
  Calendars are read from the private iCal links you give it (Google Calendar, iCloud, Outlook).
  The Alexa link and the phone alerts use ntfy, https://ntfy.sh (the public server), as a relay.
  The forecast models behind Open-Meteo's answer for Boston are NOAA's HRRR, National Blend of
    Models and GFS (US government works).
  The Glare button uses Samsung's SmartThings API (https://developer.smartthings.com) with an
    OAuth-In app the owner creates. Its sign-in passes once through httpbin.org, a public echo
    service, to show the one-time code.
  Stops, routes, station choices and counting rules follow Vestor (github.com/g-vansh/vestor).

Code written for Lucent 2.0
  The control center's server, pairing, QR encoder (ISO/IEC 18004 byte mode), iCalendar reader
  (RFC 5545 recurrence rules), rate governor, photo sandbox and SmartThings client are original
  to this project and use no libraries.

Glyphs and marks
  Every glyph (weather, bikes, docks, shuttle, aircraft, radar) and the Lucent mark are original
  drawings made for this project.

